# Line endings. This project has been worked on from macOS and from Windows,
# and git on Windows warned on every single commit that it was about to rewrite
# LF to CRLF in the working copy. Left alone, the first commit made without
# core.autocrlf set the way the previous machine had it rewrites whole files and
# buries a one-line change in a thousand-line diff.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` fixes the repository side: everything git decides is text
# is stored with LF regardless of which machine wrote it. Existing files are NOT
# rewritten by adding this — that would need `git add --renormalize .`, which is
# deliberately not done here so this commit stays reviewable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never inspects or converts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
